This package derives from JuggleIM im-web-sdk, commit
f69cbe450fc79fceac7ae24a54baee57f9b1a5c3 (version 1.9.17).
https://github.com/Juggleim/im-web-sdk

The upstream LICENSE and package metadata specify Apache-2.0. The upstream
Rollup script and generated artifact contain a MIT banner. Those original
notices are retained, without changing or resolving their differing wording.
The original source, build scripts, package metadata, lockfile and LICENSE
are available in upstream/; LICENSE is also included at package root.

DeepAgent Code modifications add durable delivery receipts, bounded protected
reader queries, exact decimal int64 decoding, immutable protected reader mode,
and typed error handling. Protected mode suppresses legacy body-bearing APIs
and notifications. It does not grant authority to execute agent tasks.
Device-bound modifications add two-step Connect challenge proofs, fixed socket
audience verification, host-signed Navigator/media HTTP requests, asynchronous
source fences, and token/proof redaction in Connect logs. The host retains
private-key custody; the SDK receives only public metadata and narrow callbacks.

The runtime is built from the readable source. Its bytes and declaration hash
are pinned in build-manifest.json. The original banner year is fixed at 2026
only during reproducible builds; the product runtime clock is unchanged.
Generated JavaScript comment whitespace is normalized before hashing. The
locked minifier retains compression with name mangling disabled to avoid its
older asynchronous scope-tracker failure.
